-    #[cfg_attr"}],"labels":["A-tokio","A-ci"],"targetBranch":"master","sourceSha":"c5d51ae876dd8a8d6519bf7d11c9169983ba7048","body":"## Motivation
Because Miri didn't have TCP socket support, the tokio tests which relied on `TcpStream`s and `TcpListener`s had to be ignored when being run with Miri. However, over the past months TCP socket support was added to Miri, so these tests no longer need to be ignored when being run with Miri. Some tests were using very small buffers or many iterations which caused them to be very slow with Miri. For the tests I considered important I've changed the buffer size/iteration count, the other tests I've annotated with `#[cfg_attr(miri, ignore)]`. A few tests using TCP sockets currently don't work with Miri, but there are open issues/PRs for those:
- `readv` can leak memory: https://github.com/rust-lang/miri/pull/5054
- Host I/O events are only processed when entering the scheduler: https://github.com/rust-lang/miri/issues/5047
